{
	"_doc": "Szadi art's RPG Worlds Desert (RPGW_Desert_v2.01): Dustwind Pass's sand, packed earth and dry scrub, the plateau's sand and rocky ledge as raised walls (raised.sandstone; walls.rock's stacked pillars are the alternative style and its loose rocks the rubble), pebbles, dirt bits and dry tufts for scatter, bush beds of the Desert's own yellow-olive scrub shrubs, a wooden fence, the plateau's cliff face for the pit walls, low rock heaps, agave and palms for the margins, narrow banner racks, piles of goods and braziers (RPG_Buildings_Desert) on the walls by the caravan stops and on the side walkways at the road's ends. The sand is lifted toward tan (blue x1.4 before the palette snap: the plateau sand's streaks otherwise snap to pale on orange and repeat as diagonal stripes); every ground cut gets the same tint so the blobs' sandy edges match, and the earth and scrub land on browns. The MainLev sheet's blobs are opaque 5 x 5 blocks (corners, edges, a 3 x 3 middle): recipe key blob9. Keys: tools/cut_tiles.py. Paths are relative to the packs dir.",
